From 828ce7924be1108f24517fc8719ea9bfe4f89363 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Dutton <chris@bigcove.io>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 00:11:16 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 10/16] docs: the firmware must be built on esp-hosted NG's
 patched Wi-Fi libraries

Stock ESP-IDF 5.5.1 lacks the beacon head/tail APPIE slots and
ieee80211_send_mgmt_internal the host-SME model relies on; a stock build
beacons nothing usable and never completes an association. Document the
esp-hosted toolchain setup and how to tell the two apart.
---
 README.md | 32 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 30 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 98787f4..2056442 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -41,11 +41,39 @@ everything above the driver - no bespoke radio API to integrate against.
 
 ## Getting started
 
-Firmware (ESP-IDF v6.0.2):
+### Firmware toolchain: ESP-IDF v5.5.1 with esp-hosted NG's Wi-Fi libraries
+
+The host-SME WiFi model (hostapd/wpa_supplicant on Linux run the AP
+authenticator and the STA SME) depends on hooks that only exist in the
+Wi-Fi libraries Espressif ships with **esp-hosted NG**, not in stock ESP-IDF:
+the `WIFI_APPIE_RAM_BEACON_PROBE_HEAD/TAIL` beacon slots and
+`ieee80211_send_mgmt_internal()` among them. A firmware built on stock IDF
+links fine but the SoftAP never beacons and clients can never associate
+(verified on hardware, 2026-10-09). Set the toolchain up exactly as
+esp-hosted does, on the same IDF commit:
+
+```sh
+git clone --branch v5.5.1 --depth 100 https://github.com/espressif/esp-idf.git ~/esp/esp-idf-v5.5.1
+cd ~/esp/esp-idf-v5.5.1
+git checkout -f fcae32885b0296b32044cb99ecbdc50d98dddb83
+git apply <esp-hosted>/esp_hosted_ng/esp/esp_driver/lib/rom.patch
+git submodule update --init --depth 1 --recursive
+./install.sh esp32c6
+rm -rf components/esp_wifi/lib/* && cp -r <esp-hosted>/esp_hosted_ng/esp/esp_driver/lib/* components/esp_wifi/lib/
+```
+
+(`<esp-hosted>` is a checkout of https://github.com/espressif/esp-hosted at
+`release/ng-1.0.6`; its `esp_hosted_ng/esp/esp_driver/.env` pins the IDF
+commit above.) A correctly built image contains the patched library's
+version string `d34ae1d`; stock IDF 5.5.1 reports `bad379d` on the ESP32's
+console at boot (`wifi firmware version:`).
+
+Build with the preset wrapper (`idf.py --preset` is an IDF 6 feature):
 
 ```sh
+. ~/esp/esp-idf-v5.5.1/export.sh
 cd firmware
-idf.py --preset production build flash monitor
+./build.sh production build        # -> build/production/trellis_radio_fw.bin
 ```
 
 Kernel module, standalone out-of-tree build:
